      "id": "q7d368q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "The Two New Union Territories Compared"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Act, 2019 reconstituted the state into two distinct Union Territories: Jammu & Kashmir, and Ladakh.",
        "The UT of Jammu and Kashmir is provided with a Legislative Assembly, whereas the UT of Ladakh is administered directly by the Centre without a legislature.",
        "Ladakh comprises the two districts of Leh and Kargil, while the UT of Jammu and Kashmir encompasses the remaining 20 districts.",
        "A common High Court continues to function as the judicial authority for both Union Territories."
      ],
      "id": "96n7oxo"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "The Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Act, 2019 bifurcated the state into two Union Territories: Jammu & Kashmir, and Ladakh.",
      "id": "29jfes1"
